---
// MCP in both directions: as a client (engine uses others' tools) and as a server (no model). Inline SVG.
---
<figure class="diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 270" role="img" aria-label="As an MCP client, your engine uses tools from other servers; as an MCP server, any client calls your tools directly with no model">
    <defs>
      <marker id="mc-ah" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L8 4L0 8z" fill="#697080"/></marker>
    </defs>

    <text x="10" y="20" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#14171f">As a client: your engine uses other tools</text>
    <g stroke="#14171f" stroke-width="1.2" fill="#fff">
      <rect x="10" y="40" width="150" height="54" rx="8"/>
      <rect x="300" y="40" width="150" height="54" rx="8" fill="#e8f3f0" stroke="#0e6b5c"/>
      <rect x="590" y="40" width="160" height="54" rx="8"/>
    </g>
    <g font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#14171f" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="85" y="63">Your engine</text>
      <text x="375" y="63">MCP client</text>
      <text x="670" y="63">MCP servers</text>
    </g>
    <g font-size="12" fill="#697080" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="85" y="81">model in the loop</text>
      <text x="375" y="81">their tools next to yours</text>
      <text x="670" y="81">HubSpot, Jira, your own</text>
    </g>
    <g stroke="#697080" stroke-width="1.3" fill="none" marker-end="url(#mc-ah)">
      <path d="M160 67H298"/><path d="M450 67H588"/>
    </g>

    <line x1="10" y1="130" x2="750" y2="130" stroke="#e3e6ec" stroke-width="1"/>

    <text x="10" y="160" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#14171f">As a server: any client calls your tools, no model</text>
    <g stroke="#14171f" stroke-width="1.2" fill="#fff">
      <rect x="10" y="180" width="150" height="54" rx="8"/>
      <rect x="300" y="180" width="150" height="54" rx="8" fill="#e8f3f0" stroke="#0e6b5c"/>
      <rect x="590" y="180" width="160" height="54" rx="8"/>
    </g>
    <g font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#14171f" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="85" y="203">Any MCP client</text>
      <text x="375" y="203">createToolServer</text>
      <text x="670" y="203">Your tools</text>
    </g>
    <g font-size="12" fill="#697080" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="85" y="221">a program or a person</text>
      <text x="375" y="221">schema · authorize · audit</text>
      <text x="670" y="221">defineTool</text>
    </g>
    <g stroke="#697080" stroke-width="1.3" fill="none" marker-end="url(#mc-ah)">
      <path d="M160 207H298"/><path d="M450 207H588"/>
    </g>
    <text x="10" y="260" font-size="12" fill="#697080">The arguments the client sends are the arguments execute receives.</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>The same protocol in both directions. Serving direct tools is how a tool becomes deterministic for any caller.</figcaption>
</figure>
